{"name":"Grape Vine","hex":"#797f5a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"grape vine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of grapevine (any sense)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grape_vine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Fisherman's knot","blocks":[{"text":"The fisherman's knot is a knot—specifically a bend—that joins two lines. The double fisherman's knot and triple fisherman's knot are variations used in climbing, arboriculture, and search and rescue. The knot is also commonly used in fishing and medicine. The difference between the three variations is the number of turns in the overhand knots that form the completed bend."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/N%C5%93ud_de_p%C3%AAcheur_double_serr%C3%A9.jpg/330px-N%C5%93ud_de_p%C3%AAcheur_double_serr%C3%A9.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fisherman's_knot"},{"title":"Gossip","blocks":[{"text":"Gossip consists of rumors or other information about the personal or private affairs of others. Gossiping is the sharing of gossip. Gossip often circulates within social groups and may serve social functions such as bonding, norm enforcement, or the sharing of reputational information. However, gossiping has often been viewed negatively by societies throughout history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Pieter_Brueghel_the_Younger_-_Proverbs_%28detail%29_-_WGA03627.jpg/330px-Pieter_Brueghel_the_Younger_-_Proverbs_%28detail%29_-_WGA03627.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gossip"},{"title":"Vitis","blocks":[{"text":"Vitis (grapevine) is a genus of about 80 species of twining plants in the family Vitaceae. The genus consists of species predominantly from the Northern Hemisphere. It is economically important as the source of grapes, both for direct consumption of the fruit and for fermentation to produce wine. The study and cultivation of grapevines is called viticulture."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Vitis_californica_with_grapes.jpg/330px-Vitis_californica_with_grapes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vitis"},{"title":"Grape","blocks":[{"text":"A grape is a fruit, botanically a berry, of the deciduous woody vines of the flowering plant genus Vitis. Grapes are a non-climacteric type of fruit, generally occurring in clusters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg/330px-Grapes%2C_Rostov-on-Don%2C_Russia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grape"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Scouting_for_girls%2C_adapted_from_Girl_guiding_-_Fisherman%27s_Knot.png/500px-Scouting_for_girls%2C_adapted_from_Girl_guiding_-_Fisherman%27s_Knot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Scouting_for_girls%2C_adapted_from_Girl_guiding_-_Fisherman%27s_Knot.png/500px-Scouting_for_girls%2C_adapted_from_Girl_guiding_-_Fisherman%27s_Knot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diagram of a single fisherman's knot","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AScouting_for_girls%2C_adapted_from_Girl_guiding_-_Fisherman's_Knot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/TripleFishermansKnot.jpg/500px-TripleFishermansKnot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/TripleFishermansKnot.jpg/1280px-TripleFishermansKnot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 